## Use one scenario to connect the layers

The supplied common journey is **valid user signs in and reaches the Account Balance view**. Use it across Android, iOS, and React Native while keeping platform-specific implementations.

| Acceptance criterion | Evidence |
| :--- | :--- |
| Valid test user can authenticate. | Controlled business-logic tests and a packaged-app journey. |
| Invalid credentials do not enter the dashboard. | A negative test with no stale authorized state. |
| Balance screen is visible and usable after successful authentication. | UI assertions and an enabled intended control, not just app launch. |
| Network/service failure does not masquerade as success. | Failure-path tests with controlled responses. |
| Logout/session change does not expose a previous user's balance. | Session isolation and stale-completion regression tests in the actual app. |

The next page will show the shared scenario through platform-specific code and tests. The examples will use explicit test doubles and existing application integration points, without inventing an Enterprise Auth SDK API.

