## Keep tests repeatable and safe

| Concern | Developer rule |
| :--- | :--- |
| Initial state | Start with known session, storage, and fixture state. Do not depend on another test running first. |
| Parallel execution | Use independent test data/accounts or an approved allocation mechanism; avoid shared mutable account state. |
| Timing | Use bounded condition waits and the framework's synchronization. Avoid fixed sleeps and automatic retries that hide failures. |
| Selectors | Verify IDs against the actual native UI/accessibility tree; do not assume one lookup works across frameworks. |
| Failure evidence | Keep useful assertion messages and sanitized diagnostics. Screenshots and videos may expose credentials or account data. |
| Side effects | Reset only test-owned data through approved fixtures. After uncertain external writes, preserve state and reconcile rather than repeat blindly. |

Real devices expose behavior that local targets may miss, but they do not guarantee all hardware compatibility. Device model/OS availability and hardware-feature support must be confirmed for the selected cloud environment. The supplied historical OS ranges are not a permanent supported-device matrix.

## Know the owners

| Owner | Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- |
| Developer | Acceptance criteria, production/test code, selectors, safe fixtures, local checks, and honest evidence. |
| Reviewer | Meaningful assertions, actual UI binding, failure coverage, isolation, and current-revision review. |
| Platform Engineering | Approved Bitrise templates, protected vendor credentials, tool pins, and integration/recovery contracts. |
| QA/test owner | Risk-based device matrix, required journeys, data isolation, triage, and suite ownership. |
| Release/security owner | Applicable assessment and TGRC approval; passing tests do not grant release authorization. |

Application PRs retain the supplied two peer approvals and required Danger/Bitrise statuses. Configuration enrollment retains its separate protected promotion process. Never expose vendor credentials to untrusted PR-controlled scripts to obtain a green test.

