## Step 1 — Define the behavior

For this example, the application owns a `SignInAndLoadBalance` use case. It calls an injected session gateway to authenticate, then loads that session's balance. Authentication failure must not request a balance; balance failure must propagate rather than return fabricated success.

The integer amount is **minor units** in this synthetic contract. Production code must preserve its approved money/currency model; never infer currency or render raw minor units as a human-readable balance.

| Case | Expected result |
| :--- | :--- |
| Authentication and balance succeed | Return the exact account data from the gateway. |
| Authentication fails | Return/throw failure; never call balance loading. |
| Balance loading fails | Propagate failure; do not fabricate zero balance. |
| Session changes during work | Actual app state owner must reject stale results; add its integration test. |

