## Step 1 — Inventory production files before measuring

List all shipped source roots, including application entry points, native modules, adapters, UI, and bootstrap code. For each platform, identify the report/tool and supported metrics. Do not omit a file simply because coverage is difficult to collect.

| Platform | Metrics and report | Required action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| React Native JS/TS | Jest/Istanbul statements, branches, functions, and lines. | Enforce all four at 100%; include all production locations. Native modules also follow native policy. |
| Android | Approved JaCoCo/Kover setup; metrics depend on the configured tool and bytecode filtering. | Enforce the approved executable scope at 100%; retain per-file/class details and explain generated-code treatment. |
| iOS | Xcode/xccov executable line coverage. | Enforce 100% executable lines for every intended production target/file; do not label this branch coverage. |

A generated file, third-party library, resource, or declaration-only file needs an explicit classification. Reviewed generated/vendor exclusions do not permit removing handwritten startup, adapters, or UI. Non-executable files need validation/review appropriate to their type; zero executable lines is not evidence of tested behavior.

If the selected tooling cannot measure a required area or metric, record the gap and owner decision. Do not present the narrower percentage as complete application coverage.

