### When the gate may pass

All required suites/device combinations must complete with acceptable assertions for the intended packages and revision. A successful upload, zero submitted suites, a skipped required test, a timed-out job, missing evidence, or an API response alone cannot establish that result. Coverage, NowSecure assessment, signing, TGRC authorization, and destination verification remain separate gates.

## 11. Diagnose failures without guessing the cause

| Symptom | Inspect first | Safe next action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Authentication error / 401 | Effective protected binding, identity, permissions, endpoint, and expiry evidence. | Ask the credential owner to investigate; do not rotate a key automatically or print it. |
| App/test package not found / 404 | Exact region, storage reference, access, actual upload receipt, and package association. | Reconcile existing state before another upload; a missing read can be inconclusive. |
| Allocation timeout | Approved criteria, current pool availability, account capacity, and actual queue result. | Record infrastructure failure; adjust only through the matrix owner. |
| Runner command missing | Approved stack/tool provisioning, path, and pinned version. | Repair reviewed tooling; do not fetch an unpinned installer during a protected run. |
| No tests discovered | Packaged test classes/runner, test filters, framework configuration, and target. | Block; do not accept an empty suite as success. |
| Element not found | Actual UI/accessibility tree, initial session, navigation state, and synchronization. | Fix selectors or state handling; do not add a fixed sleep or expose test passwords. |
| Test passes locally but fails remotely | Actual binary, device/OS, backend connectivity, permissions, signing/instrumentation, and data isolation. | Diagnose the boundary; local success does not prove cloud readiness. |
| Tests fail but Bitrise stays green | Wrapper exit handling, required statuses, and custom failure flag. | Correct the gate; never set `test_fail_on_failure: "no"` to hide regressions. |
| Test fails and evidence is absent | Failure-path collection, job IDs, safe output paths, retention, and collector errors. | Preserve the original failure; repair evidence collection without publishing raw data. |
| Upload/session creation response is lost | Candidate identity, request correlation, existing storage/job readback. | Stop writes and reconcile read-only under the one-write rule. |

Framework assertions and infrastructure failures need separate triage. Repeated success after rerunning does not erase a flaky or failed attempt. Keep the first failure evidence and fix the cause rather than using unrestricted retries.

## 12. Validate the integration before using it as a release gate

| Test condition | Expected behavior |
| :--- | :--- |
| Missing required request field | Request fails before cloud mutation. |
| Wrong platform or mismatched app/test package | Preparation or execution gate fails explicitly. |
| Unresolved native test-package storage ID | Native suite cannot start and cannot pass. |
| Wrong account/region or unavailable pool | Explicit infrastructure failure/incomplete result. |
| Required assertion fails | Framework and Bitrise gate fail. |
| No tests/required suite skipped | Required evidence remains incomplete. |
| Parallel tests share mutable account state | Isolation check fails; provision independent test data. |
| Credential or account data appears in diagnostics | Retention is blocked/sanitized under the incident/data-handling process. |
| Registration/upload/job creation becomes uncertain | Preserve, reconcile read-only, and do not replay the mutation. |
| Android passes while iOS fails | Independent platform results remain visible; overall required set is incomplete. |

