# IDE-Assisted Test Generation

Use an approved IDE assistant to help **author tests before commit**. The developer defines the scenario, supplies permitted context, reviews the draft, and verifies the behavior. Bitrise then executes the committed tests through the approved build and Sauce Labs workflow.

**Enterprise boundary:** CI never calls an LLM, generates tests, or asks an assistant to decide whether a failing test should pass. Test generation belongs to authoring; required gate decisions come from executed, reviewed code and recorded evidence.

This page applies the supplied IDE-driven testing reference. [Writing Tests](../writing-tests/) contains the full feature and platform examples; [Sauce Labs](../sauce-labs-real-device-testing/) owns cloud configuration. This workflow does not require a new AI product, plugin, or CI credential.

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Use only an Enterprise-approved assistant and permitted data context. Keep passwords, access keys, private artifact URLs, account records, raw recordings, and secret-bearing logs out of prompts. Check the actual files/context selected by the IDE. A rule file is guidance, not a data-protection control or permission to disclose confidential material.

