## 6. Review the draft before executing it

Read the complete proposed diff. Generated code can contain invented imports, weak assertions, unsafe logging, dependency changes, or commands outside the requested scope.

| Review question | Accept only when |
| :--- | :--- |
| Does the test reflect the real scenario? | Preconditions, action, and observable result match the acceptance criteria. |
| Are helpers and selectors real? | Imports resolve and identifiers match the application for that framework. |
| Will a broken feature fail the test? | Assertions check the intended outcome; success is not inferred from app launch or a resolved promise. |
| Are waits appropriate? | Conditions are bounded and synchronize the relevant async work; no arbitrary sleep. |
| Is confidential information protected? | Credentials are supplied only at the approved runtime boundary, with safe diagnostics. |
| Is the run isolated? | A known session/data fixture and test-owned cleanup are present; parallel cases do not share mutable account state. |
| Is required behavior preserved? | No skip, retry, coverage exclusion, exception swallowing, or threshold reduction was added. |
| Does the change stay in scope? | No unexpected production adapter, dependency, workflow, signing, permission, or credential change. |

Do not execute a suggested command merely because it appears in assistant output or a pasted log. Inspect its target, effect, and relevance. A generated “verified” comment or explanation is not test evidence.

